2026-09-27T07:22:13.9700933Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9701250Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9701852Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9719272Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9735557Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9759418Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9759716Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9759899Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9760280Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9760496Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9760606Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9760866Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9761052Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9761187Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9761608Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9761945Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9762595Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9763112Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9763209Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9763611Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9764124Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9764384Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9764683Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9765075Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9765162Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9765621Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9765820Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9767198Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9768710Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9768937Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9769690Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9770918Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9771882Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9772681Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9773397Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9773844Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9774428Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9774943Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9846743Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9849242Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9851424Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9852594Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9853750Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:13.9853970Z 
